content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, on the filtered-water line; this line is dosed with sodium hypochlorite (C16).",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing vibration is 7.6 mm/s. The applicable HF-300 criterion is Figure 3 for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings: 7.6 exceeds the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/D boundary and lies within the shown Zone D range of 7.1–11.0, whose instruction is 'Damage likely – stop the pump.' This is not an exact-boundary case, so the figure's unspecified boundary ownership does not affect the classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 84 °C. The manual's limits apply to housing-surface temperature: normal is up to 70 °C, alarm is 80 °C, and trip is 90 °C. Thus 84 °C is above normal and 4 °C above the alarm limit, but remains 6 °C below the trip limit; it is a high-temperature condition, not a documented 90 °C trip condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-area leakage is approximately one drop per second. This matches the manual symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal,' for which the corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No numerical allowable leakage-rate limit is supplied, so the one-drop-per-second rate cannot be compared with a documented numerical leakage limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The approximately 10-minute dry run during tank changeover exceeded the applicable operating prohibition: the HF-300 has Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and the manual states 'never run dry.' No permissible dry-run duration is documented; seal running dry is also a listed probable cause of shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: worn, cracked, or dry-run-damaged mechanical-seal faces. The troubleshooting guide explicitly associates these conditions and seal dry running with shaft-seal leakage, and this pump ran dry for about 10 minutes despite the prohibition. Additionally, if component seal HF3-450 is currently installed, this serial is within the service-bulletin population reporting early HF3-450 failures caused by a revised sleeve tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a common documented possible contributor to all three reported symptoms: shaft-seal leakage, high vibration, and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear and/or incorrect grease quantity remain possible. Bearing wear is listed under both high vibration and high bearing temperature, while over-greasing is specifically listed for high bearing temperature. Bearing condition and grease quantity have not been reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, cavitation, or an NPSH problem are secondary possible explanations for the high vibration; the supplied evidence does not distinguish among them.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-104 now and keep it stopped pending repair because the reported vibration is in Zone D. Isolate and drain the pump before beginning seal or back pull-out work.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before and during disassembly, investigate the listed causes: check grease quantity, alignment, bearings, impeller condition, and NPSH. Review the tank-changeover dry-running event. Record which seal type is installed, but do not delay the serial-specific requirement to use HF3-450B for replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Using the required lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, remove the assembly, impeller nut, and impeller. Withdraw the seal and sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and assess scoring depth; replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Inspect the bearings and impeller for the vibration and temperature causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C13",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace the drive-end and non-drive-end bearings as a pair: HF3-512 (6312-C3) and HF3-510 (6310-C3). Section 5.3 requires pair replacement when either bearing shows wear, noise, or high temperature; the reported housing temperature is above the documented alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B pre-set cartridge mechanical seal and one new HF3-120 casing gasket; do not fit HF3-450. HF3-450B needs no sleeve-setting measurement, but the sleeve scoring inspection still applies. Refit the impeller and back pull-out assembly. For Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads, tighten the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After the bearing-housing work and any movement of the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Achieve parallel offset no greater than 0.05 mm and angular misalignment no greater than 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Recommission without running dry, observing the Plan 11 seal-flush requirement. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and act on that zone; stop again for Zone D. Repeat the measurements weekly. Recheck housing-surface temperature against the 70 °C normal, 80 °C alarm, and 90 °C trip limits, and record residual shaft-seal leakage for assessment once an acceptance limit is available.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C01"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; quantity follows the single-seal pump parts list and the bulletin substitution. Mandatory replacement for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22871; gland torque 30 Nm and no sleeve-setting measurement required.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new with the seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; planned as one half of the mandatory bearing-pair replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional part—fit only if inspection shows scoring deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the immediate stop: the vibration reading is in the red Zone D, where damage is likely and the manual instructs stopping the pump. The bearing temperature being below the 90 °C trip does not override this independent stop instruction.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly or mechanical seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Treat opening and draining as work on a sodium-hypochlorite-dosed line. Obtain the site's chemical-handling, PPE, drainage, and disposal controls before opening the pump; those detailed controls are not included in the supplied evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump dry during testing or return to service. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge, and the manual explicitly prohibits dry running.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard time: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians (8.0 technician-hours).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair standard time: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians (12.0 technician-hours).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment standard time: 1.5 hours with 1 technician (1.5 technician-hours).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Arithmetic sum of the three applicable standard tasks: 11.5 task-hours and 21.5 technician-hours. This is not an outage-duration estimate; Table 6 provides no separate standard times for troubleshooting, inspections, conditional sleeve replacement, or recommissioning.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number and gland torque: the Revision D parts list identifies component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 prohibits HF3-450 and specifies pre-set cartridge HF3-450B at 30 Nm. The bulletin was issued 14 March 2026 and expressly applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-104 is HF3-22871, so the bulletin governs this asset: use HF3-450B at 30 Nm and do not use the manual's HF3-450/25 Nm combination. The manual continuation for pumps below HF3-22000 does not apply here.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apparent bearing-replacement trigger difference: the troubleshooting table says to replace bearings if worn, while the referenced section 5.3 says to replace both as a pair when either shows wear, noise, or high temperature. Section 5.3 is the specific bearing-replacement procedure and directly encompasses this reported high-temperature condition; therefore this work order replaces the pair without waiting for wear to be confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The sleeve instructions are complementary rather than a licence to omit inspection: section 5.2 requires inspection for scoring, while the bulletin's statement that no sleeve measurement is needed concerns setting the pre-set HF3-450B seal. Omit the sleeve-setting measurement, but retain the scoring inspection and apply the bulletin's greater-than-0.1 mm sleeve-replacement criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 7.6 mm/s vibration measured on Figure 3's required RMS basis, and what is the non-drive-end bearing-housing reading? Only the drive-end value is reported, while condition monitoring requires both housings and classification of the highest reading. This does not remove the conservative stop decision based on the reported drive-end value (C06, C07).",
    "What shaft-seal leakage rate, if any, is acceptable after repair? The evidence gives a corrective action for shaft-seal leakage but no numerical leakage acceptance limit for the reported approximately one drop per second (C09).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, and what is the shaft sleeve's scoring depth? The installed seal affects confirmation of the bulletin-related failure mode, and sleeve replacement depends on whether scoring exceeds 0.1 mm (C10, C13).",
    "What are the alignment readings, bearing condition, grease quantity, impeller condition, and NPSH findings? These are needed to resolve the remaining possible causes rather than assuming them (C09).",
    "What grease type and correct grease quantity apply? The troubleshooting guide requires a grease-quantity check but does not provide either specification; obtain the applicable specification rather than guessing (C09).",
    "What site PPE, chemical isolation, drain-handling, and disposal requirements apply to the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed fluid? The evidence identifies the chemical dosing but provides no detailed chemical work procedure or concentration (C16).",
    "What control failure allowed the 10-minute dry run during tank changeover, and what operating or control change will prevent recurrence? The supplied documents establish that dry running is prohibited but do not answer these asset-specific questions (C02)."
  ]
}
